        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71525",
        ":question/problem": "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{3}-x+3$ at the point $(1,4).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-x+3.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-x+3)=6{x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{'}(1)=6(1)-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{'}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{'}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$"
      },
