        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47449",
        ":question/problem": "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{2}+x$ at the point $(1,2).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{\u2032}(1)=2(1)+1=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{\u2032}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{\u2032}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"
      },
